meta {
  name: Drift Report
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/schema/{{connectionId}}/drift?against={{connectionId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  against: {{connectionId}}
  ~schema: public
}

docs {
  Procedures, functions, views and triggers in one schema that differ between this connection and `against` (same engine — MongoDB and Elasticsearch objects compare too): { schema, identical, items: [{ schema, name, kind, args?, parent?, status }] }, status different | only_left | only_right. Definitions are compared by SHA-256 of their normalized text (line endings and trailing whitespace removed); none is returned. A definition hidden on either side counts as different.

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}) plus **read** capability on **both** connections' environments — 403 otherwise.

  Errors: 400 when `against` is missing or the two connections are different engines; 503 { error, code: "CONNECTION_FAILED" }; 500 { error }.
}
